{"approved_definition": "Safety, harmony, and stability of society, of relationships, and of self. Derives from basic individual and group requirements for survival and welfare (cf. Kluckhohn, 1951; Maslow, 1965). Some security values serve primarily individual interests (e.g., health), others wider group interests (e.g., national security).", "core_value": "security", "sources": [{"entry_id": "87e92805:entry:1", "journal_entry": "My sister Graciela keeps calling to tell me I should go back to a regular job. She doesn't get it. I'm not going to sit in some warehouse again answering to a guy ten years younger than me who treats people like furniture.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "87e92805:entry:4", "journal_entry": "Motorcycle started making a noise yesterday. A grinding thing when I brake. I took it to Raul's shop and he looked at it and said the brake pads are gone and the disc is warped, it needs replacing. He quoted me a number that wiped out everything I'd saved from the Alfredo job. Every peso.

I stood there in Raul's shop and felt my stomach just drop. Because it's not optional — the motorcycle is how I make deliveries. Without it I'm on foot or taking the subte, which means fewer trips, which means less money, which means next month's rent gets tight. It's like this chain where one thing breaks and everything behind it starts wobbling. I told Raul to do it, because what choice do I have. But I walked home and I couldn't even eat dinner.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "87e92805:entry:0", "journal_entry": "Started doing the math again tonight. If I keep the delivery app running five days a week and pick up at least two handyman jobs on the weekends, I can cover everything with about twelve thousand pesos left over. That leftover is supposed to be for the motorcycle insurance renewal in May. I wrote it on a sticky note and put it on the fridge next to the old one that says "DO NOT touch savings."

Funny thing is, I spent Saturday at the parrilla with Cacho and Pocho like always, and the bill came out heavier than usual because we ordered that tira de asado. I didn't blink. Six hours of good food and good talk, what am I going to do, skip it? Some weeks the numbers work, some weeks they don't. But I'm not going to stop living just because the spreadsheet says I should.", "nudge_response": null}], "user_phrase": "Feeling calm and secure in my life"}
